-- a digest that differs across an admissible proton transfer is not the restriction of any function on
-- the substance: given one such pair, no function out of the tautomer carrier agrees with it on the
-- forms. So InChI's partial tautomer invariance is not a tolerance to be tightened; it is the report
-- that the digest is a function on chosen representatives and not on the substance at all (IUPAC project
-- 2012-023-2-800, open since 2012; 26.25% and 13.46% invariance over the tautomeric part of the CSD).
taut-no-lift : (A : Type 0) → (step : A → A → Bool) → (d : A → Nat) → (a : A) → (b : A) → isTrue (step a b) → (d a ≡ d b → Empty) → ((g : Taut A step → Nat) → ((x : A) → g (taut-pt x) ≡ d x) → Empty)
taut-no-lift A step d a b p no =
  λ g → λ agrees → no (concat (sym (agrees a)) (concat (taut-respects A step Nat g a b p) (agrees b)))
